dtfile.msg: leave out the two usage messages over the catalogue limit.

Set 18 messages 23 and 24 are dtfile's usage text, already split in two
upstream (1048 and 1060 bytes). A System V catalogue message holds at most 1024 bytes (NL_TEXTMAX), and
gencat refuses the whole file for one longer message. The C catalogue
leaves them out, with a comment; catgets then returns the program's
built-in text, which is the same text (for message 24 the built-in text is the
better one: the catalogue has a stray "/" in "-tree_files /never/always/
choose"). A translated catalogue
cannot carry them while the limit stands.

